// Title: Potential PowerShell Execution Policy Tampering - ProcCreation
// Sigma ID: cf2e938e-9a3e-4fe8-a347-411642b28a9f
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment
// Description: Detects changes to the PowerShell execution policy registry key in order to bypass signing
//   requirements for script execution from the CommandLine
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/de-de/powershell/module/microsoft.powershell.security/set-executionpolicy?view=powershell-7.3
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_registry_set_unsecure_powershell_policy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\ShellIds\\Microsoft.PowerShell\\ExecutionPolicy" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ExecutionPolicy") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "Bypass" or ProcessCommandLine contains "RemoteSigned" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Unrestricted")
